      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Prescribing recommended medications is associated with improved outcomes in coronary artery disease patients. Likewise, adherence to prescribed medications, which frequently appears far from optimal, is significantly correlated with improved survival in \"real world\" observational databases. The present article reviews currently available data on the impact of medication adherence on outcomes in patients with coronary artery disease."},
